*******************************************************************************
* cap_cmomi - 2-terminal ngspice wrapper around the Verilog-A (OSDI) compact model
*             (ihp-sg13cmos5l port: reduced Metal1..Metal4 thin-metal stack)
*
* Copyright 2026 IHP PDK Authors
* Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License").
*
*******************************************************************************
* *** APPROXIMATE MODEL -- NOT YET VALIDATED ON ihp-sg13cmos5l SILICON ***
* Coefficients are TRANSFERRED from the sg13g2 characterisation (thin metals
* M1..M5) and re-used on the
* cmos5l M1..M4 stack BY LAYER COUNT N = mmax-mmin+1.  NONE are measured on
* cmos5l silicon; N=2 is additionally extrapolated.  One exception: the
* two feed terms (feed='same' and feed='double') are fitted in-house on the cell
* as drawn, because the g2 characterisation used a feed structure this PCell does not
* draw; they carry no layer keying.  See the Cfeed block in cap_cmomi.va.  Treat all results as
* engineering estimates; a re-fit is pending silicon (~3-6 months).  Shipped so
* designers can simulate a physically-reasonable cap_cmomi today.
*******************************************************************************
*
* Interdigitated metal-oxide-metal capacitor on the cmos5l thin-metal stack
* (Metal1..Metal4).  Full RF equivalent circuit; coefficients keyed by layer
* count N = mmax-mmin+1 (N=2 extrapolated, N=3,4 g2-measured-transferred), the
* two feed terms excepted as noted above.
*
* The Verilog-A device cap_cmomi is 3-terminal (PLUS, MINUS, SUB); SUB is the
* substrate reference for the oxide shunt.  This subckt keeps the classic
* 2-terminal interface by tying SUB to global ground 0.
*
* Requires the OSDI object to be loaded first (done in libs.tech/ngspice/.spiceinit):
*   osdi $PDK_ROOT/$PDK/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/cap_cmomi.osdi
* Build it with libs.tech/verilog-a/openvaf-compile-va.sh.
* Simulator scope: ngspice via OSDI (built with -D__NGSPICE__).  Xyce / gnucap /
* qucs-s are not wired and would need a separate Verilog-A build per simulator.
*
* feed token: string 'none'|'same'|'double' -> numeric code (0|1|2) for the
* Verilog-A.  w,l in metres; mmin/mmax metal indices (1=Metal1 .. 4=Metal4).
* m: parallel device multiplier (ngspice subckt multiplier).  mm_ok: accepted for
* interface parity but a NO-OP -- cap_cmomi has no characterised mismatch model.
*******************************************************************************
* STATISTICAL / CORNER MODELING (known caveat, to address with silicon):
* cap_cmomi has NO characterised process-corner or mismatch variation.  The
* Verilog-A density coefficients are the g2-derived NOMINAL values, so cap_cmomi
* returns the same nominal capacitance in every corner (typ/bcs/wcs) and in
* Monte-Carlo (no local mismatch).  This is NOT a claim that the device is
* corner-stable; the spread is simply not modelled.  Extracting it needs silicon
* matched-pair / array test structures, deferred to a future test chip.  Treat
* corner/MC results for cap_cmomi as nominal.
*******************************************************************************
* RF VALIDITY WINDOW (full fit-validity note in the Verilog-A header):
* the low-frequency capacitance is the trustworthy quantity across the drawn size
* range.  The RF branches (series R/L, skin, substrate shunt) are lumped fits valid
* to ~50 GHz.  For the DEFAULT feed=double, LARGE devices (l~60um, or ~30x30)
* self-resonate in-band (~30-47 GHz) against a two-sided SRF the g2 fit does
* not cover -- treat the default-feed SRF near/above those frequencies as an
* unvalidated prediction.  feed=same/none stay capacitive well past 50 GHz.
*******************************************************************************
.param none=0 same=1 double=2

.subckt cap_cmomi PLUS MINUS w=5e-6 l=5e-6 mmin=1 mmax=4 feed=double subblock=0 mm_ok=1
.param m=1
Ncap PLUS MINUS 0 cap_cmomi_mod w={w} l={l} mmin={mmin} mmax={mmax} feed={feed} subblock={subblock} m={m}
.model cap_cmomi_mod cap_cmomi
.ends cap_cmomi
